-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and the answers used below`

`1 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2026
`3 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 3 3 2026
`17 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 17 3 2026
`18 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 18 3 2026
`20 Dec 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 20 12 2026
`27 Dec 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 27 12 2026
`3 Jan 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 3 1 2027
`10 Jan 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 1 2027
`15 Feb 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 2 2027
`20 Feb 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 20 2 2027
`1 Mar 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2027
`2 Mar 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 3 2027
`15 Mar 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2027
`15 Feb 2028` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 2 2028
`29 Feb 2028` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2028
`14 Mar 2028` MEANS `the calendar date` 14 3 2028

`SPOUSE` MEANS `their spouse or de facto partner immediately before the death`
`CHILD` MEANS `their son or daughter`
`PARENT` MEANS `their parent`
`SIBLING` MEANS `their brother or sister`
`OTHER` MEANS `someone else (another relative, a friend, a carer)`

`SNOK A` MEANS `yes: you are the senior next of kin as the spouse or de facto partner (s 3, paragraph (a))`
`SNOK B` MEANS `yes: you are the senior next of kin as a son or daughter aged 18 or over (s 3, paragraph (b)); any other available adult son or daughter is so equally`
`SNOK C` MEANS `yes: you are the senior next of kin as a parent (s 3, paragraph (c)); the other parent, if available, is so equally`
`SNOK D` MEANS `yes: you are the senior next of kin as a brother or sister aged 18 or over (s 3, paragraph (d)); any other available adult brother or sister is so equally`
`SNOK E` MEANS `yes: you are the senior next of kin as the appropriate person under the customs and tradition of the community or group to which the person who died belonged (s 3, paragraph (e))`
`SNOK F` MEANS `yes: you are the senior next of kin as a person whose relationship with the person who died the coroner considers sufficient (s 3, paragraph (f))`
`NOT SNOK` MEANS `no: on these facts you are not the senior next of kin (s 3, a "means" definition: the text's no)`

`in NT` MEANS `in the Territory: the body is in the Territory, or the death or its cause occurred there`
`outside, resident` MEANS `outside the Territory, and the person ordinarily lived in the Territory`
`outside, not resident` MEANS `outside the Territory, and the person did not ordinarily live in the Territory`

`violent` MEANS `it appears unexpected, unnatural or violent, or to have resulted directly or indirectly from an accident or injury`
`during anaesthetic` MEANS `it occurred during an anaesthetic`
`from anaesthetic` MEANS `it occurred as a result of an anaesthetic and is not due to natural causes`
`natural` MEANS `none of these: an expected death from natural causes`

`no care` MEANS `not held in care`
`CEO care` MEANS `a child in the CEO's care under the Care and Protection of Children Act 2007`
`mental health custody` MEANS `a patient in custody under the Mental Health and Related Services Act 1998, in a hospital or temporarily removed from one`

`no custody` MEANS `not held in custody`
`police` MEANS `in the custody or control of a Territory police officer`
`AFP` MEANS `in the custody or control of a member of the police of a State or another Territory, or of the Australian Federal Police`
`prison` MEANS `detained in a custodial correctional facility (a prison)`
`youth detention` MEANS `detained in a detention centre approved under the Youth Justice Act 2005`
`escaping` MEANS `being taken into, or escaping from, any of that custody, control or detention`
`detained under a law` MEANS `detained anywhere in the Territory by a person authorised to do so under any Act or law in force there, including Commonwealth law`
`escaping detention under a law` MEANS `escaping from such detention in the Territory`

`REPORTABLE A` MEANS `yes: a reportable death under paragraph (a) of the definition in s 12(1)`
`REPORTABLE B` MEANS `yes: a reportable death under paragraph (b) of the definition in s 12(1): a Territory resident who died outside the Territory, the cause of death not certified by a medical practitioner there`
`NOT REPORTABLE` MEANS `no: not a reportable death (s 12(1), a "means" definition: the text's no)`

`MUST REPORT` MEANS `yes: you must report it as soon as possible to a coroner or a police officer (s 12(2); maximum penalty 40 penalty units), and then give the coroner any information that may help the investigation (s 13(1); maximum penalty 40 penalty units)`
`NO GROUNDS` MEANS `no duty under s 12(2): you do not have reasonable grounds to believe that it has not been reported (the text's no)`
`NO DUTY NOT REPORTABLE` MEANS `no duty under s 12(2): not a reportable death on these facts (the text's no)`

`MUST INVESTIGATE` MEANS `yes: the coroner to whom the death was reported must investigate it (s 14(2))`
`NEED NOT, ELSEWHERE` MEANS `the coroner need not investigate it, because an investigation or inquest is held in a State or another Territory (s 14(3)); the coroner still may`
`NOT YET REPORTED` MEANS `not yet: s 14(2) binds the coroner to whom the death is reported, and it has not been reported; a person with reasonable grounds to believe it has not been reported must report it (s 12(2))`
`NOT REQUIRED, NOT REPORTABLE` MEANS `not required by s 14(2): not a reportable death on these facts (the text's no); a coroner has jurisdiction only if it appears to the coroner that the death is or may be a reportable death (s 14(1))`

`MANDATORY` MEANS `yes: the coroner must hold an inquest (s 15(1))`
`CARE AND CUSTODY` MEANS `on the words of s 15(1)(a) ("held in care and custody") an inquest is mandatory only for a person held in both care and custody, and your relative was held in only one; if "and" is read as "or", as in s 12(1)(vii), the coroner must hold one; otherwise the coroner may hold one as he or she thinks fit (s 15(2))`
`UNLAWFUL KILLING` MEANS `the coroner may hold an inquest if he or she thinks fit, because the coroner suspects unlawful killing (s 15(1A)); it is not mandatory`
`DISCRETIONARY` MEANS `not mandatory: the coroner may hold an inquest as he or she thinks fit (s 15(2), (3)); a decision not to hold one must be notified to the senior next of kin with reasons, and may be taken to the Supreme Court within 14 days (s 16)`
`NO INQUEST` MEANS `no inquest under this Act on these facts: not a reportable death, so on these facts the coroner has no jurisdiction to investigate it (ss 14(1), 15; the text's no)`

`TOLD` MEANS `yes: the coroner must record the decision and its reasons in writing and, as soon as practicable, notify you of it in writing with the reasons (s 16(1)); you then have 14 days to apply to the Supreme Court (s 16(2))`
`MAY BE TOLD` MEANS `the coroner may notify you but need not: the duty is to notify the senior next of kin (s 16(1)(c)); the Act says no more (NOTHING-kind)`
`NO DECISION` MEANS `s 16 does not arise: the coroner has not decided not to hold an inquest (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

`APPLIED IN TIME` MEANS `in time: you applied within 14 days after receiving notice of the decision (s 16(2)); the Supreme Court may order that an inquest be held if it thinks fit (s 16(3))`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `still in time: you have not applied, and the 14 days after receiving notice of the decision have not ended; apply by the last day (s 16(2))`
`OUT OF TIME 14` MEANS `out of time: the 14 days after receiving notice of the decision have passed (s 16(2), the text's no); a coroner may still hold an inquest if satisfied that new facts or evidence make it necessary or desirable (s 44A(1))`
`14 NOT BEGUN` MEANS `the 14 days have not begun: they run from receiving the written notice of the decision not to hold an inquest (s 16(2))`

`CONTROL S17(2)` MEANS `yes: the body is under the coroner's control until a certificate permitting its disposal is issued (s 17(1)); and because the Supreme Court has ordered an inquest under s 16(3), the coroner or clerk must not issue that certificate (s 17(2), which on its words sets no end to the bar)`
`CONTROL S21(4)` MEANS `yes: the body is under the coroner's control until a certificate permitting its disposal is issued (s 17(1)); and the Supreme Court's order prohibits disposal until the coroner has the autopsy results and has ordered disposal (s 21(4)(b))`
`CONTROL` MEANS `yes: the body is under the coroner's control until the coroner or coroner's clerk issues a certificate permitting its disposal (burial or cremation) (s 17(1))`
`RELEASED` MEANS `no: a certificate permitting disposal has been issued, which ends the coroner's control under s 17(1) (the text's no: "until")`
`NO CONTROL` MEANS `s 17 does not put the body under the coroner's control: not a reportable death on these facts, or the body is not in the Territory (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

`IN 48` MEANS `in time: you apply within 48 hours after receiving the notice, as the section allows`
`OUT 48` MEANS `out of time: more than 48 hours have passed since you received the notice (the text's no: a period the text fixes)`
`48 NOT BEGUN` MEANS `the 48 hours have not begun: they run from receiving the written notice`
`48 SNOK ONLY` MEANS `the section gives this application to the senior next of kin; it says nothing of an application by anyone else (NOTHING-kind)`
`NO REFUSAL` MEANS `nothing to apply against: the coroner has not refused an autopsy that you asked for (s 21(3) runs from a refusal)`
`NO DECISION OR ORDER` MEANS `nothing to apply against: no autopsy decision or exhumation order has been made`

`ADVISED` MEANS `yes: the coroner must take reasonable steps to advise you of the direction to perform an autopsy (s 22)`
`NOT IN CUSTODY` MEANS `not under s 22: the person who died was not a person held in custody (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`NOT DIRECTED` MEANS `not under s 22: no autopsy has been directed (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`S22 SNOK ONLY` MEANS `s 22 is a duty to the senior next of kin; it says nothing of advising anyone else (NOTHING-kind)`

`AUTOPSY BARRED BY COURT` MEANS `no: the Supreme Court has ordered that no autopsy be performed (s 23(3))`
`AUTOPSY WAIT FOR NOTICE` MEANS `not yet: the coroner must first give you written notice of the decision (s 23(1)), and the autopsy must not be performed until 48 hours after you have been given it (s 23(2))`
`AUTOPSY WAIT 48` MEANS `not yet: the autopsy must not be performed until 48 hours after you were given notice of the coroner's decision (s 23(2)); within those 48 hours you may apply to the Supreme Court to stop it (s 23(3))`
`AUTOPSY 48 PASSED` MEANS `s 23(2) no longer holds it back: 48 hours have passed since you were given notice of the decision (the text's no: "until")`
`AUTOPSY IMMEDIATE` MEANS `s 23(2) does not hold it back: the coroner believes the autopsy needs to be performed immediately (s 23(2), "unless")`
`AUTOPSY NO REQUEST` MEANS `s 23(2) does not hold it back: no request not to direct an autopsy has been made by the senior next of kin (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`NO AUTOPSY` MEANS `no autopsy is in question: the coroner has not decided that an autopsy is necessary`

`EXHUME BARRED BY COURT` MEANS `no: the Supreme Court has ordered that the body not be exhumed (s 24(4))`
`EXHUME WAIT NOTICE` MEANS `not yet: at least 48 hours' written notice must be given to you before the body is exhumed (s 24(2)); within 48 hours after receiving it you may apply to the Supreme Court to stop it (s 24(4))`
`EXHUME WAIT REQUEST` MEANS `not yet: you asked the coroner not to exhume the body, and it must not be exhumed until 48 hours after your request (s 24(3))`
`EXHUME FREE` MEANS `s 24 no longer holds it back: the notice has run its 48 hours (or the coroner was satisfied it could not be given), and any request of yours not to exhume was made 48 hours ago or more`
`NO EXHUMATION` MEANS `no exhumation is in question: the coroner has not ordered one`
`EXHUME SNOK ONLY` MEANS `s 24's notice and request are the senior next of kin's; the section says nothing of anyone else (NOTHING-kind)`

`ADVERTISED IN TIME` MEANS `yes: the inquest was advertised not less than 14 days before it (s 37)`
`ADVERTISED LATE` MEANS `no: the inquest was advertised less than 14 days before it (s 37, the text's no)`
`STILL TIME TO ADVERTISE` MEANS `not yet advertised, and there is still time: the clerk must publish it by the latest day (s 37)`
`TOO LATE TO ADVERTISE` MEANS `not yet advertised, and the latest day has passed: it can no longer be advertised not less than 14 days before the inquest (s 37, the text's no)`

`TAKE PART` MEANS `yes: you may appear or be represented, call and examine or cross-examine witnesses, and make submissions (s 40(3)); the coroner may also make available to you a statement it intends to consider (s 40(2))`
`NO OPINION` MEANS `s 40(3) gives these rights to a person the coroner considers has a sufficient interest; the coroner has not formed that opinion of you, and the Act says no more (NOTHING-kind)`

`CANNOT REFUSE` MEANS `no: once the coroner has offered you a certificate, you are no longer entitled to refuse on the ground that your answer may incriminate you (s 38(2)); when you have given evidence the coroner must give you the certificate`
`NO OFFER` MEANS `the coroner has not offered you a certificate under s 38(1); s 38 does not take away a refusal on the ground of self-incrimination, and the Act says no more (NOTHING-kind)`

`criminal` MEANS `criminal proceedings against me (other than for perjury)`
`civil` MEANS `civil proceedings against me`
`tribunal` MEANS `proceedings against me before a tribunal or a person acting judicially`
`perjury` MEANS `a prosecution of me for perjury`
`someone else` MEANS `proceedings against someone else`
`PROTECTED` MEANS `no: with a certificate under s 38, a statement you made in answer to a question as part of that evidence is not admissible against you in these proceedings (s 38(3))`
`PERJURY` MEANS `s 38(3) does not protect it on a prosecution for perjury ("other than"); the Act says no more (NOTHING-kind)`
`NOT AGAINST YOU` MEANS `s 38(3) protects you only in proceedings against you; for proceedings against someone else the Act says no more (NOTHING-kind)`
`NO CERTIFICATE` MEANS `without a certificate under s 38, the Act gives your answers no protection and says no more (NOTHING-kind)`

`SUPPRESS` MEANS `yes: the senior next of kin's request makes the name a sensitive personal matter, and since the coroner believes publishing the report would disclose it, the coroner must order that the report not be published (s 43(1)(c)); publishing in breach carries up to 85 penalty units or 2 years' imprisonment (s 43(2))`
`NO BELIEF` MEANS `no order is required by s 43(1)(c): the coroner does not reasonably believe that publishing the report would disclose the name (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`NO REQUEST` MEANS `the senior next of kin has not asked; s 43(1)(c) then does not make the name itself a sensitive personal matter, and the Act says no more about it (NOTHING-kind); the other grounds in s 43(1) may still apply`

`NEW INQUEST GROUND` MEANS `yes: you may apply to the Supreme Court (s 44(1)), and you rely on a ground on which, if satisfied, the Court may declare findings void and order a new or re-opened inquest (s 44(2), (3)); the Act sets no time limit`
`NO GROUND` MEANS `you may apply (s 44(1)), but the Court may make the order only if satisfied of a ground in s 44(3), and you rely on none (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`NO INQUEST HELD` MEANS `s 44 is about the findings of an inquest, and none has been held; against a decision not to hold one see s 16(2) (14 days), and a coroner may hold one on new facts or evidence (s 44A(1))`

`as evidence` MEANS `as evidence of a matter it records (for example, the cause of death or how the death happened)`
`other use` MEANS `for another purpose (for example, to show that the coroner made a finding, or what was said)`
`RECORD BARRED` MEANS `no: the coroner's record of findings, evidence and comments is not admissible as evidence of a matter contained in it (s 11(2), the text's no)`
`RECORD OTHER` MEANS `s 11(2) bars only using the record as evidence of a matter contained in it; for another use the Act says no more (NOTHING-kind)`

`CORONER NOT WITNESS` MEANS `no: a coroner must not be called to give evidence in a court or judicial proceedings about anything learned as coroner (s 45(1), the text's no)`
`CORONER OFFENCE` MEANS `s 45(1) does not apply to proceedings against a coroner for an offence (s 45(2)); the Act says no more (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin`

-- (a): the spouse or de facto partner immediately before death.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `SPOUSE` 40 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SNOK A`
-- (b): an adult child, no spouse available; at 18 exactly, and at 17 (no, not (f) without the coroner's opinion).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `CHILD` 18 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SNOK B`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `CHILD` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT SNOK`
-- A 17-year-old child, nobody else available, the coroner considers the relationship sufficient: (f).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `CHILD` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `SNOK F`
-- An adult child, a spouse available: the spouse ranks first.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `CHILD` 30 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT SNOK`
-- (c): a parent, no spouse and no adult child available; a sibling available does not matter.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `PARENT` 60 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SNOK C`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `PARENT` 60 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT SNOK`
-- (d): an adult sibling, nobody ahead available; at 17 no; with a parent available no.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `SIBLING` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SNOK D`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `SIBLING` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT SNOK`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `SIBLING` 25 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT SNOK`
-- (e): the appropriate person by custom for an Aboriginal person, even with a spouse available (fork F1).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `OTHER` 50 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SNOK E`
-- The spouse of an Aboriginal person is senior next of kin under (a) even if someone else is the customary person.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `SPOUSE` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `SNOK A`
-- Customary standing does not count if the person who died was not Aboriginal.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `OTHER` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT SNOK`
-- (f): nobody under (a) to (e) available and the coroner's opinion; not if a parent is available, or a customary person
-- is available for an Aboriginal person; a customary person counts only for an Aboriginal person.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `OTHER` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `SNOK F`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `OTHER` 45 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT SNOK`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `OTHER` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOT SNOK`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `OTHER` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `SNOK F`
#ASSERT `s 3 -- am I the senior next of kin` `OTHER` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT SNOK`

§ `s 12 -- is it a reportable death`

#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT REPORTABLE`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT REPORTABLE`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `during anaesthetic` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `from anaesthetic` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `CEO care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `mental health custody` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `prison` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `AFP` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `youth detention` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `escaping` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `detained under a law` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `escaping detention under a law` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `no custody` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `REPORTABLE A`
-- (b): a Territory resident who died elsewhere, not certified there; certified, no; violent but certified, no (no link
-- to the Territory for (a)); a non-resident dying elsewhere, no.
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `outside, resident` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REPORTABLE B`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `outside, resident` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT REPORTABLE`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `outside, resident` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT REPORTABLE`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- is it a reportable death` `outside, not resident` `violent` `no care` `prison` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT REPORTABLE`

§ `s 12 -- must I report the death`

#ASSERT `s 12 -- must I report the death` `in NT` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `MUST REPORT`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- must I report the death` `in NT` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NO GROUNDS`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- must I report the death` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO DUTY NOT REPORTABLE`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- must I report the death` `outside, resident` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `MUST REPORT`

§ `s 14 -- must the coroner investigate`

#ASSERT `s 14 -- must the coroner investigate` `in NT` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `MUST INVESTIGATE`
#ASSERT `s 14 -- must the coroner investigate` `in NT` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NEED NOT, ELSEWHERE`
#ASSERT `s 14 -- must the coroner investigate` `in NT` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT YET REPORTED`
#ASSERT `s 14 -- must the coroner investigate` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT REQUIRED, NOT REPORTABLE`
#ASSERT `s 14 -- must the coroner investigate` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT REQUIRED, NOT REPORTABLE`

§ `s 15 -- must there be an inquest`

-- (a) on its words: held in care and custody.
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `natural` `mental health custody` `police` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `MANDATORY`
-- Held in custody only, or care only: the "care and custody" reading (finding; fork F5).
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `prison` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CARE AND CUSTODY`
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `natural` `CEO care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `CARE AND CUSTODY`
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `police` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `CARE AND CUSTODY`
-- (b) injuries in custody; (c) identity unknown.
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `violent` `no care` `no custody` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `MANDATORY`
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `prison` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `MANDATORY`
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `MANDATORY`
-- (1A) unlawful killing suspected; otherwise s 15(2).
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `UNLAWFUL KILLING`
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `DISCRETIONARY`
-- A resident's uncertified death elsewhere: reportable, but no Territory link for s 15(1) or (1A).
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `outside, resident` `violent` `no care` `no custody` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `DISCRETIONARY`
#ASSERT `s 15 -- must there be an inquest` `in NT` `natural` `no care` `no custody` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO INQUEST`

§ `The regulative rule alone`

#ASSERT `applying at this time is in time` 14 0
#ASSERT `applying at this time is in time` 14 13
#ASSERT `applying at this time is in time` 14 14
#ASSERT NOT (`applying at this time is in time` 14 15)
#ASSERT `applying at this time is in time` 14 (0 MINUS 3)
#ASSERT `applying at this time is in time` 48 48
#ASSERT NOT (`applying at this time is in time` 48 49)

§ `s 16 -- decision not to hold an inquest`

#ASSERT `s 16 -- must I be told of a decision not to hold an inquest` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `TOLD`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- must I be told of a decision not to hold an inquest` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `MAY BE TOLD`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- must I be told of a decision not to hold an inquest` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NO DECISION`

-- The last day: 14 days after receipt; across a year end; to 29 February in a leap year; to 1 March otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 16 -- the last day to apply for an inquest` `3 Mar 2026` EQUALS `17 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- the last day to apply for an inquest` `20 Dec 2026` EQUALS `3 Jan 2027`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- the last day to apply for an inquest` `15 Feb 2028` EQUALS `29 Feb 2028`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- the last day to apply for an inquest` `15 Feb 2027` EQUALS `1 Mar 2027`

#ASSERT `s 16 -- am I in time to apply for an inquest` TRUE `3 Mar 2026` TRUE `17 Mar 2026` `1 Mar 2027` EQUALS `APPLIED IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- am I in time to apply for an inquest` TRUE `3 Mar 2026` TRUE `18 Mar 2026` `1 Mar 2027` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME 14`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- am I in time to apply for an inquest` TRUE `3 Mar 2026` TRUE `3 Mar 2026` `1 Mar 2027` EQUALS `APPLIED IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- am I in time to apply for an inquest` TRUE `3 Mar 2026` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` `1 Mar 2027` EQUALS `APPLIED IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- am I in time to apply for an inquest` TRUE `3 Mar 2026` FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `17 Mar 2026` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- am I in time to apply for an inquest` TRUE `3 Mar 2026` FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `18 Mar 2026` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME 14`
#ASSERT `s 16 -- am I in time to apply for an inquest` FALSE `3 Mar 2026` FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `18 Mar 2026` EQUALS `14 NOT BEGUN`

